error[ffi_tag_is_a_union]: `fixedbugs-2137-union-tag.h` declares `u` as a `union`, not a struct — C keeps the two in one namespace and will not let one stand for the other
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2137-a-value-only-the-probe-sees-is-told-beside-a-record-holding-a-union-tag.hero:12:18
     |
  12 |     record U tag u  #~ ffi_tag_is_a_union
     |                  ^
  note: a `tag` names a struct (§4.19), and a `record` binds a union only by a typedef's name, as `record W` over `typedef union { … } W;` does. If `fixedbugs-2137-union-tag.h` gives `u` a typedef, bind that name; if not, give it one in a header of the program's own, `typedef union u U;`, and bind `record U`, or reach it as a `ptr` through C functions

error[ffi_constant_type]: `K_DIV` in `fixedbugs-2128-values.h` cannot be declared `i64`: clang refuses the header's value at line 4: its expression holds an operation C leaves undefined for the operands it is given, and the program's own unit, built with clang's checks for an overflow, a shift, a division by zero and a float out of an integer's range, traps where it reads it
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2137-a-value-only-the-probe-sees-is-told-beside-a-record-holding-a-union-tag.hero:19:5
     |
  19 |     constant K_DIV: i64  #~ ffi_constant_type
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: `fixedbugs-2128-values.h` line 4 reads `#define K_DIV ((-2147483647 - 1) / -1)`
  note: an operation C leaves undefined gives no value: wherever C computes it, a program reading `K_DIV` reads whatever the machine held. A group's `constant` is the value C computes from the header (§ 13): correct the value there, or bind a constant whose value C defines
